# Right-hand QWERTY mirror drills for GNU Typist.
# These drills assume Karabiner maps held Space plus right-side keys to
# the corresponding left-side QWERTY letters.

B: Right-hand QWERTY mirror

T:This lesson practices normal QWERTY output while your right hand
 :uses the Karabiner Space layer.
 :
 :Tap Space by itself for a normal space. Hold Space while pressing
 :right-side keys to type the mirrored left-side letters.
 :
 :Useful mirror pairs:
 :
 :y->t  u->r  i->e  o->w  p->q
 :h->g  j->f  k->d  l->s  ;->a
 :n->b  m->v  ,->c  .->x  /->z
 :6->5  7->4  8->3  9->2  0->1

I:Home row targets. Type the shown letters; use held Space
 :for letters that live on the left side of QWERTY.
d:asdf fdsa asdf fdsa
 :jkl; ;lkj jkl; ;lkj
 :asdf jkl; asdf jkl;
 :fads lads salad salsa
 :fall lass adds alas

I:Top row targets.
 :Keep the rhythm slow and even.
d:qwer rewq qwer rewq
 :uiop poiu uiop poiu
 :qwer uiop qwer uiop
 :tree were queue power
 :quiet write route quote

I:Bottom row targets.
 :Use accuracy first; speed comes later.
d:zxcv vcxz zxcv vcxz
 :m,./ /.,m m,./ /.,m
 :zxcv m,./ zxcv m,./
 :vex buzz cove cave
 :brave civic exact zebra

I:Number row targets.
 :Hold Space for the mirrored left-side numbers.
d:12345 54321 12345 54321
 :67890 09876 67890 09876
 :12345 67890 54321 09876
 :11223 44556 77889 99001

I:Short word drills.
 :These words emphasize the mirrored left side.
d:fade fade fade
 :read read read
 :safe safe safe
 :vast vast vast
 :craft craft craft
 :brave brave brave
 :treat treat treat
 :queue queue queue

I:Mixed word drills.
 :Stay relaxed; restart with ESC if the layer gets confusing.
d:fade read safe vast
 :craft brave treat queue
 :cave vex zebra exact
 :quiet write route quote
 :fall lass salad salsa

I:Short sentence practice.
 :This is still practice-only.
s:a brave craft worker can read a safe route.
 :a quiet zebra can vex a vast crowd.
 :write a clear draft and treat errors as data.
 :read the queue, save the state, and craft a fix.

T:End of right-hand QWERTY mirror drills.
 :
 :Run this lesson again with:
 :
 :  gtypist-right-hand-qwerty

